### Recursos (modalidad JWT). Un recurso es el par (method, path) con la ruta EN PATRÓN.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@token = <access_token>

### getAll: el catálogo completo (87 recursos sembrados)
GET {{baseUrl}}/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### getOne
GET {{baseUrl}}/resources/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### create: punto de acceso nuevo (verbo y ruta se normalizan) -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "get",
  "path": "/api/reports/settlements/:id/",
  "description": "Reporte de liquidación"
}

### create: (method, path) ya existe -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "POST",
  "path": "/api/weighings"
}

### create: ruta que no es un patrón de la API -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "reportes"
}

### PATCH -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/resources/88
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Reporte de liquidación por id"
}

### deactivate: ningún rol puede ya autorizar ese endpoint
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/resources/88/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### delete (físico); 409 si está concedido a algún rol
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/resources/88
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
